linearComb -- generic linear combination of elements
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        linearComb(L,varName)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of vector fields or
        differential forms, see *note DiffAlgField: DiffAlgField, or *note
        DiffAlgForm: DiffAlgForm,
      * varName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, name of the generic
        coefficient
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note DiffAlgElement: DiffAlgElement,, generic
        linear combination of the list L

Description
===========

This routine produce a generic linear combination of the elements in L. It can
be used together with *note genKer: genKer, or *note genIm: genIm, to solve a
system of homogeneous linear equations.



In this example we compute a generic and a particular linear combination of two
particular differential 2-forms.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : w = random newForm(2,1,2,"a")                                           |
|                                                                             |
|        2             2                            2            2            |
|o1 = (2x  - 2x x  + 6x  - 3x x  + 6x x )dx  + (- 7x  + 5x x  - x  - 2x x  -  |
|        0     0 1     1     0 2     1 2   0        0     0 1    1     0 2    |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
