logarithmicForm -- creates a logarithmic form
*********************************************

  * Usage: 
        logarithmicForm(n,L,varName)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of variables minus one
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of degrees
      * varName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, name of the
        coefficients
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Projective: logarithmicForm_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmProjective=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, whether to create a logarithmic form that descends to projective
        space
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note DiffAlgForm: DiffAlgForm,, a generic
        logarithmic form

Description
===========

A logarithmic form of type (d_0,...,d_n) is a differential 1-form w that can be
written as w=(prod f_i)sum df_i/f_i, where f_i is a polynomial of degree d_i.
This routine creates such a logarithmic form using homogeneous polynomials.
When using a list L of length two, the differential form is called rational.



In this example we generate a random logarithmic form in affine 3-dimensional
space with degrees (1,1,2).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : random logarithmicForm(2,{1,1,2},"a")                                   |
|                                                                             |
|           2          2      3       2                     2           2     |
|o1 = (- 30x x  + 20x x  + 10x  + 600x x  - 395x x x  - 220x x  - 100x x  +   |
|           0 1      0 1      1       0 2       0 1 2       1 2       0 2     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|           2       3           3      2          2      2                    |
|     405x x  - 100x )dx  + (30x  - 20x x  - 10x x  - 95x x  + 80x x x  +     |
|         1 2       2   0       0      0 1      0 1      0 2      0 1 2       |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        2          2        2      3              3       2           2      |
|     30x x  + 10x x  - 60x x  + 15x )dx  + (- 600x  + 490x x  + 140x x  -    |
|        1 2      0 2      1 2      2   1          0       0 1       0 1      |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|        3       2                    2           2        2                  |
|     30x  + 100x x  - 415x x x  + 60x x  + 100x x  - 15x x )dx               |
|        1       0 2       0 1 2      1 2       0 2      1 2   2              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : DiffAlgForm                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In this example we generate a generic rational form in the projective plane of
type (1,1).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : logarithmicForm(2,{1,1},"a",Projective => true)                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = ((a0 a2 a1  - a1 a0 a2 )x  + (a0 a2 a1  - a1 a0 a2 )x )dx  + ((-        |
|         1  0  1     0  1  1  1      1  0  2     0  1  2  2   0              |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     a0 a2 a1  + a1 a0 a2 )x  + (a0 a1 a2  - a0 a1 a2 )x )dx  + ((- a0 a2 a1 |
|       1  0  1     0  1  1  0      1  2  1     1  1  2  2   1         1  0  2|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     + a1 a0 a2 )x  + (- a0 a1 a2  + a0 a1 a2 )x )dx                         |
|         0  1  2  0        1  2  1     1  1  2  1   2                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : DiffAlgForm                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In the following example, we produce a logarithmic form that descends to
projective space.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : l = random logarithmicForm(2,{1,1},"a",Projective => true)|
|                                                               |
|o3 = (9x  - 11x )dx  + (- 9x  - 19x )dx  + (11x  + 19x )dx     |
|        1      2   0        0      2   1       0      1   2    |
|                                                               |
|o3 : DiffAlgForm                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (radial 2)_l                                              |
|                                                               |
|o4 = 0                                                         |
|                                                               |
|o4 : DiffAlgForm                                               |
