File: DiffAlg.info, Node: substitute_lpDiffAlgElement_cmRing_rp, Prev: singularIdeal, Up: Top

substitute(DiffAlgElement,Ring) -- gets the RingElement of a differential form or vector field in a ring
********************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note substitute: (Macaulay2Doc)substitute,
  * Usage: 
        sub(e,R)
  * Inputs:
      * e, an instance of the type *note DiffAlgElement: DiffAlgElement,, a
        differential form or vector field
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the target ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, an element of R
        representing e

Description
===========

By its nature, the package *note DiffAlg: Top, is constantly changing the rings
where its differential forms and vector fields are defined. This function is
useful to get information of *note DiffAlg: Top, out to some common polynomial
rings and work with the rest of Macaulay2 packages.



In this example we get the singular locus of a logarithmic form and compute its
Hilbert polynomial.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : w = random logarithmicForm(2,{1,1},"a",Projective => true)|
|                                                               |
|o1 = (35x  + 21x )dx  + (- 35x  + 7x )dx  + (- 21x  - 7x )dx   |
|         1      2   0         0     2   1         0     1   2  |
|                                                               |
|o1 : DiffAlgForm                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = singularIdeal w                                       |
|                                                               |
|o2 = ideal (35x  + 21x , - 35x  + 7x , - 21x  - 7x )           |
|               1      2       0     2       0     1            |
|                                                               |
|               QQ[i]                                           |
|o2 : Ideal of ------[][x ..x ]                                 |
|               2        0   2                                  |
|              i  + 1                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S = QQ[gens ring I]                                       |
|                                                               |
|o3 = S                                                         |
|                                                               |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hilbertPolynomial (sub(I,S))                              |
|                                                               |
|o4 = P                                                         |
|      0                                                        |
|                                                               |
|o4 : ProjectiveHilbertPolynomial                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note substitute(DiffAlgElement,Ring):
    substitute_lpDiffAlgElement_cmRing_rp, -- gets the RingElement of a
    differential form or vector field in a ring
